    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, that's great question. So Chris had reached out to us through a letter and introduced himself to and said if there's anything ever that we wanted to do or if there's anything that he could do to please let him know. And right away, I said to Marcy, I said listen, he's reaching out asking if there's anything that we can do. I think we should take him up on it. And him and Mary came out to our house, spent I would say probably a good two hours at our house, talking about what had happened to Samantha, why this was important to us, what transpired. In South Carolina, we had a vigil that we were asked, I was asked to speak at, and then there was a metavigil when we came home, right in our hometown. And right away, I made it, I had said that it was our mission to make rideshare safety a priority. And so that nobody ever goes through this again and reaching out to Congressman Smith, we sat and talked, as I mentioned, and really it was like, what can we do? What is there to do when we started working on a bill and legislation immediately? and it brings us to where we are today, working with the Congress and the Senate, working with Uber, working together as a team, and really trying to accomplish and make things safer for the rideshare industry.",
