    "turn_idx": 19,
    "turn_text": "Uber has actually put out some data. It took a lot to get more transparency. But in just a two year time period, just almost 6,000 sexual assaults occurred, 18 murders. And the problem is that many drivers, we don't know how many, in the rideshare industry, and that's Uber, Lyft, and many others, a lot of smaller ones, just have not properly vetted, in many cases, their drivers. So, somebody thinks they're getting in the backseat and is very safe. Well, we will take in the bill the best available technology, including numbers that could be transferred to the potential rideshare occupant. It's all about confirming before you get in the door and close the door, of the vehicle, that this is the vehicle you've asked for. And then there's a record that adds to the transparency and the accountability. Uber has announced that they're doing the numbers. So again, you would verify by a number that this is indeed who you think it is.",
