    "turn_text": "Well, when New Jersey did pass it, and they did it within a month of, and they really used our bill and the great input that was provided for our bill and for theirs by the justices, they have a March 1st must be implemented by. So we're just about a month away from full implementation. So a lot of setup is going on. The Attorney General was very involved as our others, the head of the DMV. So all of it's in place to have a launch for implementation. And that's why we want to work faster on this one. We introduced this more than eight months ago. We've run into barriers, but I think those barriers, one by one, are being overcome. We've got the disability groups like the National Federation of the Blind, who see this as a very significant means of protecting their community, and they're the ones who were very strong on saying a QR code can't be used by a person blind. So a number of sequence offers an opportunity for them to verify that this is their ride making it again. You can't make it totally safe. We want to make it safer, and this will make it significantly safer. And the Josephson deserve credit because of their advocacy. A lot of the companies, particularly Uber, are stepping up and doing a lot of things proactively, I believe, and I believe this totally, that would not have happened without their concern for",
